    "description": "A configuration engine keeps its own small expression language for 700 rule files: literals, identifiers, unary and binary operators with precedence and parentheses. The current reader is a 400-line regex chain that fails with 'syntax error near 14' and no position context; a precedence bug shipped to production because nobody could review the chain. The team needs the language to grow (function calls, optional chaining) while keeping error messages precise (offset, expected token) and keeping the grammar readable for reviewers. Hand-rolling the reader is preferred over a parser generator so the build stays dependency-light. The decision to implement: how to read the expression language into a tree with explicit precedence handling and recoverable, position-carrying errors.",
    "decision_statement": "Read the expression language into a syntax tree with explicit precedence and position-carrying errors.",
    "notes": "Pratt parser stays acceptable for the precedence-climbing variant the reviewer may prefer."
